 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Post color-attenuated classification
-An algorithm that rapidly evaluates the optical properties of each segment by eliminating the extinction coefficient from the opacity-associated color integral and computing color attenuation segment by segment instead of point by point [S2]. This approach improves lookup table generation speed and accuracy compared to point-wise integration, often used in GPU-based raycasting implementations.
