 ## Background
-The method originates from the analysis of 3D Gaussian Splatting rendering accuracy. It was formally proven in the supplemental material of "Does 3D Gaussian Splatting Need Accurate Volumetric Rendering?" by Celarek et al. [S1]. The proof demonstrates that the complex volume rendering integral for a Gaussian primitive simplifies to a closed-form expression involving the exponential of the projected 2D density. This insight is critical for understanding the trade-offs between accurate volumetric rendering and the simplified splatting approximations used in real-time 3DGS.
